From: Structure Robot <robot@localhost>
To: Alice Loopback <alice@localhost>, Bob Loopback <bob@localhost>
Subject: Four levels deep, with a preamble
Message-ID: <nested-0004@localhost>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: multipart/mixed; boundary="OUTER-=_1"

This is the preamble. It sits between the headers and the first boundary and
must never appear in any part's body. MIME-unaware readers see this text.

--OUTER-=_1
Content-Type: multipart/related; boundary="REL-=_2"; type="multipart/alternative"

--REL-=_2
Content-Type: multipart/alternative; boundary="ALT-=_3"

--ALT-=_3
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 7bit

The plain text alternative, three levels down: mixed > related >
alternative > text/plain.
--ALT-=_3
Content-Type: text/html; charset=utf-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: quoted-printable

<html><body><p>The <b>HTML</b> alternative, with an inline image:</p>
<img src=3D"cid:pixel-0004@localhost" alt=3D"a pixel"></body></html>
--ALT-=_3--

--REL-=_2
Content-Type: image/png
Content-Transfer-Encoding: base64
Content-ID: <pixel-0004@localhost>
Content-Disposition: inline; filename="pixel.png"

iVBORw0KGgoAAAANSUhEUgAAAAEAAAABCAYAAAAfFcSJAAAACklEQVR4nGMAAQAABQABDQottAAA
AABJRU5ErkJggg==
--REL-=_2--

--OUTER-=_1
Content-Type: text/csv; charset=us-ascii; name="numbers.csv"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: base64
Content-Disposition: attachment; filename="numbers.csv"

bmFtZSxjb3VudAphbHBoYSwxCmJldGEsMgpnYW1tYSwzCg==
--OUTER-=_1--

And this is the epilogue, after the closing delimiter. It is not a part
either, and a parser that treats it as one grows a phantom attachment.
`,
